# agnostic-ai

> Keep one editable set of instructions and settings in `.agnostic-ai/`.
> Run `agnostic-ai sync` to write each coding tool's configuration files.
> Supported tools use different paths and formats, including `CLAUDE.md`,
> `AGENTS.md`, `GEMINI.md`, and `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`.

A spec is a source file for an instruction, task, or setting. A target is a
coding tool selected in `agnostic-ai.yaml`. Edit sources, preview changes,
sync, and check the result with `agnostic-ai sync --check`. A passing check
means generated files match the sources; tool support differs by spec kind
and field. Read the selected tool's guide before relying on a restriction.

The command runs locally and is MIT licensed. It supports {{.Supported}} coding tools,
with {{.Default}} enabled by default. Select only the tools the project uses. Follow
the installation guide for the method and version your project needs.

For setup or migration, follow agent-setup.txt. For an existing configured
checkout, keep its targets, install its documented version, run sync, and
check the result. Do not initialize it again or edit generated tool files.
Fetch the guide for your task first. Use llms-full.txt when you need the
complete user documentation.

